fxsound-linux (0.4.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release. The microphone runs in a lane of its own beside
    the speakers', with noise suppression at three levels and in three
    channel modes, an adaptive de-esser, de-reverb, echo cancellation and a
    calibration wizard; applications can keep a preset of their own; a
    running instance answers on D-Bus as org.fxsound.FxSound, `--watch`
    streams what changes and `--self-test` checks an installation. See the
    upstream changelog in /usr/share/doc/fxsound-linux/changelog.gz.
  * Installs the D-Bus activation file, so a call to org.fxsound.FxSound
    starts FxSound through the systemd user unit; the tray's three status
    icons under hicolor's scalable/status, without which the tray showed a
    blank; and the AppStream metainfo, so software centres list it.
  * The manual page is packaging/fxsound.1 now, the one every package ships.
  * Recommends a file-chooser backend for the portal (xdg-desktop-portal-gtk,
    -kde or -gnome), which xdg-desktop-portal alone does not provide, and
    dbus-user-session, which gives a compositor started from a tty the
    session bus the tray, the notifications and the D-Bus interface need.
  * debian/copyright gives the RNNoise code and model under
    crates/fxsound-rnnoise (BSD-3-Clause), the Noto fallback faces (OFL-1.1)
    and the Gilroy faces a stanza each, with their notices and licences,
    where it declared every file AGPL-3.0-or-later.
  * debian/rules keeps a RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN the caller has already set.

 -- FxSound Linux port contributors <blackixxce12@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 27 Sep 2026 14:09:18 +0400

fxsound-linux (0.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian packaging, tracking upstream 0.3.0.
  * The release that gives a microphone a chain of its own: denoise, high-pass,
    downward expander, equalizer, de-esser, compressor, makeup gain and a
    look-ahead limiter, separate from the music path. See the upstream
    changelog in /usr/share/doc/fxsound-linux/changelog.gz.
  * Ships the factory and bonus .fac presets and the TOML voice presets under
    /usr/share/fxsound/presets, which is one of the two prefixes the binary
    searches (crates/fxsound-preset/src/store.rs:65); installing them anywhere
    else gives a working application with an empty preset list.
  * The systemd user unit is installed but deliberately not enabled. The
    desktop entry already starts FxSound, and having both would put two
    instances in a race for the control socket in $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/fxsound.
    Enable it by hand with `systemctl --user enable --now fxsound` if you want
    it to come up with the session instead.

 -- FxSound Linux port contributors <blackixxce12@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 21 Sep 2026 02:00:00 +0400
